"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and a phase one budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate to leverage AI research. The team has expanded with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, including an onboarding session on September 10th. Key milestones include gathering R&D proposals by July 20th to enhance data visualization tools, completing the testing phase (celebrated on October 10th), and moving into the development phase led by Omar Jensen. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November."
